course: dictionary
lesson: 11833
title: The blahs and blah, blah, blah
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how you feel, even when nothing has gone wrong. In American talk, «the blahs» is a word for feeling bored, tired or a little fed up, with no clear reason. You can usually spot it from the clues around it: nothing bad happened, but the person just feels flat.
explain: «Blah, blah, blah» is a different use. It is said when talk is boring or empty, and not worth repeating. Comics and stories use it to skip over words that would be dull to read. Look at who is speaking and how they say it, and the meaning often becomes clear.
explain: Check your guess by putting it into the sentence. «Ben had the winter blahs» works if you swap in bored and tired with no clear reason. If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. If not, look for more clues or ask a grown-up.
fact: The blahs is an informal noun, used mostly in American everyday talk.
fact: «The winter blahs» means feeling bored, tired or fed up during the dark, grey months.
fact: The blahs is a feeling without a clear cause, so nothing bad has to have happened.
fact: «Blah, blah, blah» means boring or empty talk that is not worth repeating.
fact: «Blah» on its own is informal; it is the same word that appears in «blah, blah, blah».
exercise: «Ben had the winter blahs. He felt tired and bored, but nothing bad had happened.» What does the blahs mean? | *A feeling of being bored, tired or fed up, with no clear reason | Very loud singing | A big party for the winter | A bad cold with a sore throat
exercise: «Stop with the blah, blah, blah, said Sam. I want to play!» What does blah, blah, blah mean here? | A kind of cake | *Boring or empty talk that is not worth repeating | A song about the sea | Very fast running
exercise: Mum says, «It is so grey outside that I think I have the blahs.» Which feeling is closest to the blahs? | *Fed up and a bit flat | Overjoyed | Dizzy and sick
test: «Ava had the blahs all week, so she stayed in bed and read.» What does the blahs suggest about Ava? | She had a broken leg | She was very excited about a trip | She was cold and wet from the rain | *She felt bored and tired, with no clear reason
test: In a comic, a character says «blah, blah, blah» while the others yawn. Why does the author write it? | To show the room is very noisy | To show a character is singing a song | To show someone is counting out loud | *To show the talk is boring and not worth repeating
exam: «The winter blahs made Lily quiet at dinner, but she was not ill.» Why is Lily quiet? | She is bored and fed up with no clear cause | *She feels bored and flat, with no clear reason | She is shouting at her friends | She has a cold and cannot talk
